abstract: >
  The Archimedes Project is a 5-year independent research program
  toward a self-improving AGI substrate. This thesis documents the
  project as a coherent research monograph, presenting the ENWI
  framework (5-layer architecture, 11 mathematical theorems, 5
  falsifiable predictions) and the Y0/Y1 research results. Highlights
  include the H1 decoupling ablation (5/5 seeds, frozen Monitor AUROC
  0.796 vs joint 0.072 on LunarLander-v3), the Slot-Monitor (AUROC
  0.989 vs raw-history 0.796), the Y1.3 training-time regularizer
  (n=15, +50 mean over PPO baseline, p<0.001), the DLR attention
  architecture (4 envs, 97.8% mean accuracy), and the 9-hypothesis
  pre-registered framework (6 validated, 2 refuted, 1 open).
  Honest null results (8 pre-reg H tests, 0 supported at the strict
  t>2.0 rule) are documented with the same precision as positive
  results. The thesis closes with a 5-year roadmap toward a
  verifiable, open, reproducible AGI substrate.
